{
  "_readme": [
    "Seed list of Singapore employers for the sourcing pipeline (DESIGN.md section 4).",
    "This is DATA, not code (CLAUDE.md rule 4): nothing here may be hardcoded in lib/.",
    "",
    "`type` groups employers by how they hire, which is the useful axis - a US tech",
    "company staffs Singapore as an APAC sales base, a regional platform staffs product",
    "here. The 2026-09-23 sourcing run found 185 Singapore roles across 27 US tech boards",
    "and exactly 2 were product roles; that finding is what `type` exists to capture.",
    "",
    "`ats`, `token` and `probed` are FILLED IN by `npm run boards:probe` - do not hand-edit",
    "them. `ats: \"unknown\"` means no public JSON board was found, so the careers page needs",
    "the HTML route or a manual check.",
    "",
    "`careersUrl` is the human-facing careers page. Add companies freely.",
    "",
    "`confirmed: true` marks a board a human has verified. Corroboration is strict and",
    "produces false negatives (lever/nium is really Nium - its postings name Instarem,",
    "its subsidiary - but nothing in the payload proves it). Confirmed entries are kept."
  ],
